  "summary": "editor.api.history.undo() and redo() return HistoryResult synchronously; a replay that waits on an effect owner returns { status: 'pending', settled } whose settled never rejects. HistorySettlement, HistoryOutcome, HistoryResult and HistoryApi are root plitejs exports. An owner or settlement failure after the claim settles failed, keeps the entry, clears pending and reports once through lifecycleErrorSink, then reportError, then console.error. An owner result is asynchronous only when it has a callable then, so a non-object result settles failed and a then-undefined result settles in the call; an owner promise from another realm goes pending. The mounted runtime keeps its timing and focus guards and checks the claim version History records. About 370 call sites dropped void or await. This execution applies the diff panel's round-2 patch on the owner's go, without a panel review of that patch, and completes the work the partial execution record left open.",
